-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 67: add the Track U.3 materialization fields to the `cites`
--   (source → source) edge table.
--
-- Background — two different states, one robust migration. On STAGING the
-- `cites` table was already correctly
--   DEFINE TABLE cites TYPE RELATION IN source OUT source SCHEMAFULL
-- (verified via INFO FOR DB / INFO FOR TABLE, 2026-06-27) — defined at runtime by
-- the relation write path, NOT by the migration suite. On a FRESH migration-only
-- container, however, `cites` comes up as the SurrealDB default
--   DEFINE TABLE cites TYPE ANY SCHEMALESS
-- (the migration suite never defined it). So `cites` is in the SAME class as the
-- `mentions` drift migration 66 fixed: correct on staging, undefined-as-relation
-- on a fresh DB. This migration therefore ASSERTS the relation definition (so it
-- is correct everywhere) AND adds the U.3 materialization fields — mirroring
-- migration 66's non-destructive OVERWRITE remediation exactly.
--
-- The U.3 fields. On a SCHEMAFULL table, RELATE-with-SET of an UNDEFINED field is
-- silently dropped — so the regenerator's `confidence` / `reference_text` /
-- `match_method` would vanish unless first DEFINEd. This adds exactly those three
-- (plus `created_at` for parity with migration 66's `mentions`) so a materialized
-- cites edge carries its precision provenance: the match confidence, the verbatim
-- cited reference text, and which precision path (`doi` / `title_author`)
-- resolved it.
--
-- Strategy: DELETE null-endpoint junk + OVERWRITE only (mirrors migration 66).
--   1. DELETE only null-endpoint junk rows (in = NONE OR out = NONE). A real
--      `cites` edge always has non-null in/out, so this is a no-op on a healthy
--      table and only clears the non-edge junk a drifted TYPE ANY table could
--      hold (which would otherwise block the RELATION redefine). A blanket
--      `DELETE cites` would WIPE healthy edges — the destructive mistake migration
--      58 made; 62/66 fixed it with this null-endpoint-only predicate and 67
--      follows suit.
--   2. DEFINE TABLE OVERWRITE ... TYPE RELATION FROM source TO source. On
--      SurrealDB v2 OVERWRITE converts a drifted TYPE ANY table to RELATION; on an
--      already-correct RELATION table it re-asserts the identical definition and
--      PRESERVES existing edge records (the migration-62/66 empirical fact). The
--      `cites` table holds 0 rows on staging (no intra-corpus citations until
--      Track V — U.1) and the regenerator owns the edge set (clear + recreate),
--      so there is nothing to back-fill.
--   3. DEFINE the edge fields with OVERWRITE (additive; the pre-existing ontology
--      fields are left as-is).
--
-- Strict-field / S.4 prevention note (mirrors migration 66). Every field added
-- here is strict-typed WITH a DEFAULT, so a row written without it does not error
-- — the regenerator always supplies `confidence` / `reference_text` /
-- `match_method` explicitly via RELATE-with-SET, and the DEFAULTs are a safety
-- floor, never the live value. Adding a strict field with no default to a table
-- that already holds rows is the S.4 hazard; this table is empty AND every field
-- has a default, so the hazard does not apply. The fix is forward-safe.
--
-- Idempotent + forward-only: every OVERWRITE re-asserts an identical definition.
-- Down is a documented no-op (see 67_down) — dropping the fields would only
-- re-break the U.3 regenerator's writes (the very gap this fills) and the cites
-- edge table is a regenerated projection with no canonical state worth a
-- destructive rollback.
-- ============================================================================

-- 1. Drop ONLY null-endpoint junk rows (the non-edge records a drifted TYPE ANY
--    table could hold). Real `cites` edges always have non-null in/out, so this
--    never touches them — no-op on the empty staging table AND on any healthy
--    edge set.
DELETE cites WHERE in = NONE OR out = NONE;

-- 2. Re-assert the canonical edge definition. Converts a drifted TYPE ANY table
--    to RELATION source->source on v2; identical no-op (edges preserved) on an
--    already-correct RELATION table.
DEFINE TABLE OVERWRITE cites SCHEMAFULL TYPE RELATION FROM source TO source;

-- 3. U.3 materialization fields. `confidence` is the matcher's confidence (1.0 for
-- a DOI-exact hit, else the blended title+author score). `reference_text` is the
-- verbatim cited reference (the ParsedReference.raw_text) so a reviewer can see
-- exactly what matched. `match_method` records the precision path that resolved
-- the edge (`doi` | `title_author`) — the per-edge "why", parallel to
-- `mentions.concept_name`.
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE confidence ON cites TYPE float DEFAULT 0.0;
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE reference_text ON cites TYPE string DEFAULT "";
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE match_method ON cites TYPE string DEFAULT "";
DEFINE FIELD OVERWRITE created_at ON cites TYPE datetime DEFAULT time::now();

-- Index on confidence so the viz / triage can threshold edges (mirrors
-- migration 66's idx_mentions_weight). OVERWRITE so a re-apply converges.
DEFINE INDEX OVERWRITE idx_cites_confidence ON cites FIELDS confidence;
